@hagakure_eth If you have an approval open, it grants access for that contract to move the approved asset on your behalf. No transaction needed from your wallet, which is why these things are exposed.

@printer_brrr @hagakure_eth Tough to fall asleep, as you can imagine.

It's determined by how the contracts are designed. On Uniswap, every action must be initiated by you because you're always swapping a token for another in the moment. If they had something like limit orders, which other platforms do, then the architecture would be different, and it would be able to fulfill your order at any time, given a certain price.

Same with NFTs. If you list a board ape for 10 ETH with a 2-week expiration, then you obviously do not need to transact for somebody to fulfill that listing, which moves your board ape at a later time. The approval handles that for you. It's just the architecture of the marketplace.

